{
 "name": "material_inheritance_parity",
 "face_ring_start": "ignored",
 "face_ring_start_note": "The cases that only RETAG faces keep every ring and every ring start, and they declare \"compared\" one by one below. The six that also split, merge or spin a face inherit that command's own ring-start behaviour, which is unported (see doc/tasks/backlog/1311-ring-start-laws-to-capture.md); this fixture is about which faces carry which material, so it takes the rotation-tolerant reading for those rather than freeze a start nobody has read.",
 "description": "Which faces still share a material after the topology under them is rewritten -- merge, split, spin, vertex split and paste. The material VALUES are never compared across the seam (the two engines name surfaces differently); the PARTITION they induce is.",
 "source": "frozen reference capture (task 1121, nine-tool sweep)",
 "provenance": {
  "schema": 1,
  "source": "live-capture",
  "reference": "ref-editor@11.2v3",
  "method": "command",
  "captured_utc": "2026-08-18",
  "harness": "tools/local/capture (tasks 1121/1123)",
  "task": "1160",
  "notes": "Nothing in either engine's suite asked this before. The reversed cell is the control that settled the law: tagging the far face first and merging with the near one selected first still yields the LOWEST-INDEX face's tag, so selection order decides nothing. CHANNELS: the sweep's comparison was never vertex-only -- it compared the vertex multiset, the edge multiset, faces BOTH as ordered rings (winding shows) and as unordered position sets, the material partition, the per-face 'did this face's own tag change', and the post-command selection. Re-checked independently over all 215 frozen cases: ZERO agree on vertices while differing on ordered face rings, so nothing frozen here is a vertex-channel-only agreement. PRECISION: the sweep compared at 1e-4 and this fixture's tolerance matches it. The actual reproduction is far tighter -- 208 of the 215 cases are bit-identical at the dumps' 6 decimals and the remaining 7 agree to 3e-6 or better, that being the worst deviation anywhere in the set. The tolerance is the MEASUREMENT's bound, not the data's."
 },
